# public/build is deliberately NOT ignored. The shipped image carries no Node toolchain, so the
# compiled assets have to be in the repository or a fresh clone renders no page at all — which is
# exactly what happened before this line was written. CI asserts they match the source.
/public/fonts-manifest.dev.json
/public/hot
/public/storage
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
/vendor
_ide_helper.php
Homestead.json
Homestead.yaml
Thumbs.db

# The VitePress build and its cache. Unlike public/build, this is NOT committed: the docs are
# published by CI to the marketing host rather than served from this repository, so a checked-in
# build would be a large diff on every edit that nothing ever reads.
/docs/.vitepress/dist
/docs/.vitepress/cache

# A working copy of the private Cloud overlay, if somebody has put one here.
#
# This repository is public. The overlay is not: it holds billing, the managed key service and the
# per-organisation storage implementations. A `git add -A` in a checkout that happens to contain one
# would publish the lot, and a force-push does not un-publish anything on GitHub.
#
# The overlay is meant to be mounted at /var/www/overlay and installed from a path repository, not
# copied in here. See .ddev/docker-compose.overlay.yaml.
/cloud/
